    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.00) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66), our two premier plays of the day. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits immensely from a favorable encounter with Cavalli, combining a robust base projection with a 14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage and a premium leadoff spot. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is positioned for a high-ceiling performance against Bassitt; his score is buoyed by favorable park factors and the strategic advantage of hitting in the #2 hole. We are also monitoring **Heliot Ramos** (65.50), whose projection assumes a #5 slot; his high score is driven by a strong matchup against Severino in a park that heavily favors his profile, though we must confirm his status once the official lineup drops.\n\nOur roster strategy today prioritizes speed and efficiency, leading to a difficult decision at the bench. **Coby Mayo** (44.15) was the closest to cracking the starting lineup, ultimately edged out by **Liam Hicks** and **Miguel Vargas**. While **Coby Mayo** offers power, his projection was penalized by a lower-tier batting order position (#8), which restricted his expected run-scoring opportunities compared to the higher-order stability provided by **Liam Hicks** and **Miguel Vargas**. We continue to manage our bench depth carefully as we await the return of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Kyle Tucker** from their respective absences, which will necessitate future roster consolidation.\n\nRegarding situational risks, **Jackson Merrill** (52.77) faces the day's toughest test against the elite arm of Logan Gilbert (xERA 2.98). While his dynamic platoon advantage provides a floor, this matchup requires close monitoring; he is currently our lowest-scored starter. Conversely, **Sam Antonacci** (63.68) remains a high-value play despite a mediocre park factor, as his elite xwOBA of 0.402 and lead-off status provide a significant cushion against the moderate threat posed by Taillon. We have elected to bench **Nolan Schanuel** due to a neutral platoon disadvantage against Wrobleski, choosing to lean into the offensive momentum of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (59.27) in the utility spot to maximize our chances in the R/RBI categories.",
